sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant UI as Browser
    participant HTTP as Django ASGI / async iterator
    participant P as Producer thread
    participant G as Gemini API
    participant R as Redis broker / result backend
    participant W as Laptop Celery worker
    participant T as Watcher thread
    participant DB as Django AILog
    participant L as Redis event LIST
    UI->>HTTP: Authenticated POST /api/v1/chat/stream/
    HTTP->>P: Start synchronous generator through bridge
    Note over P,W: Discovery is also a Celery job; omitted here for clarity
    P->>G: Prompt + tool declarations
    G-->>P: Text and/or function call
    P-->>HTTP: tool_start through asyncio.Queue
    HTTP-->>UI: SSE frame
    P->>R: tools.get_weather on laptop.tools
    R->>W: Deliver named task with kwargs
    P->>T: Start watch_job daemon thread
    par Laptop execution
        W->>R: update_state(PROGRESS, msg)
        W->>W: Run sequential provider calls
        W->>R: Final result / terminal state
    and Backend observation
        loop Poll until ready (sleep 0.1 seconds)
            T->>R: Read latest state and metadata
            T->>DB: Save newly observed message
            T->>L: RPUSH tool_log; EXPIRE 120
            P->>L: BLPOP, idle wait up to 30 seconds
            L-->>P: Next observed tool_log
            P-->>HTTP: Hand off SSE text through asyncio.Queue
            HTTP-->>UI: tool_log SSE frame
        end
    end
    T->>R: Get final result
    T->>DB: Save Done! log
    T->>L: Push completed tool_log with output
    L-->>P: Final tool_log
    P-->>HTTP: Final tool_log then tool_done
    HTTP-->>UI: SSE frames
    P->>G: function_response with result
    G-->>P: Answer text
    P-->>HTTP: Text chunks then done
    HTTP-->>UI: Final SSE frames
    Note over T,L: Current failure path also labels errors completed; not a recommended contract
    Note over HTTP,UI: Bundled chat.js lacks tool_log handling; receiving is not the same as displaying
